node_modules/
.pi/npm/
# Slate runtime state (worker transcripts, episodes, pending handoff) —
# session data must never be committed.
.pi/slate/
# pi's transient lock on the project settings file — a directory it creates and
# removes around every read of .pi/settings.json. A session (or a verification
# run) that is killed outright can leave one behind, and it must never be
# committed. The glob covers a file as well as a directory.
.pi/*.lock
# Per-track implementer reports are untracked workflow working material.
/track-*-implementer-report.md
# IDE state
.idea/
# NOTE: package-lock.json is COMMITTED and is deliberately not ignored here.
# It was ignored while the four pi SDK packages existed only as peerDependencies
# at "*": npm resolved them to whatever was current locally, so a lockfile would
# have pinned that drift and misled the reader. Tier-1 CI removed that premise.
# The same four packages are now ALSO exact-pinned in devDependencies (0.83.0),
# so the lockfile records a version this repo chose, not one it happened to get,
# and `npm ci --ignore-scripts` — what the workflow runs — needs the file to
# exist. See AGENTS.md § Packaging rules, "The devDependency carve-out".
